WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.590
"Moments later, it started to become clear.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.450
Someone was trudging through the water behind
us and coming for our boat."

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:22.640
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.930
splash of red sauce.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.080
My name is CZ, and I will be your server this
episode.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.920
Today’s story is set at the happiest place
on earth.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.690
But even the happiest places have a dark side.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:37.910
Let's dig right in.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:47.449
Sean: “Come on Tom, let’s go!

00:00:47.449 --> 00:00:50.629
Let’s go!”

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:52.579
Hear that annoying voice rushing me out the
door?

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:54.949
That’s my little brother Sean.

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:59.429
Today I’d be responsible for escorting Sean
and his friend Nick, to Disneyland for his

00:00:59.429 --> 00:01:00.429
birthday.

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:04.470
Sure, I wasn’t looking forward to getting
up early, nor was I looking forward to keeping

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.660
an eye on two 11 year olds all day, but I
have to admit, I was kind of excited to spend

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.660
the day at Disney.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:15.160
It had been a long time my parents had taken
me there, so I was kind of looking forward

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:20.159
to revisiting the likes of Space Mountain,
Haunted Mansion and of course: Pirates of

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:21.659
the Caribbean.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:25.870
What I hadn't taken into account, was that
my brother had never been to Disney, so although

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:30.619
he was excited, when we actually got there
and he saw the size of everything, Sean became

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:32.250
a little bit more timid.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.190
We had to work our way up to the more exciting
attractions.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.189
For me, this was a bit of a drag.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:41.490
I wasn’t exactly looking forward to riding
Peter Pan or Buzz Lightyear when I told my

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.850
mom I would take him to the park for the day.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.060
And while I do admit that the Buzz Lightyear
ride is actually pretty fun, I made sure to

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.729
gradually acclimate him to the thrill rides
as well, starting with the Gadget Go Coaster

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:58.100
to Big Thunder and eventually hitting Matterhorn
Bobsleds and even Space Mountain.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.859
It was getting close to dusk when I suggested
we check out Pirates of the Caribbean.

00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:04.170
Sean had been hesitant about it all day.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:08.150
I tried to explain that it was much tamer
than Space Mountain or any of the coasters

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.710
we had been on that day.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.230
But he resisted.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:15.000
There is something about being in a boat and
being in the dark that didn't sit well with

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.000
him.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.720
But with a little arm twisting, and with the
added element of him not wanting to look like

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:24.630
a pussy in front of his friend, I was able
to get Pirates on our agenda that evening.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.550
As we queued, I could see my brother starting
to get nervous.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.771
He does this thing where he runs his hands
through his hair when he's nervous, and right

00:02:30.771 --> 00:02:32.930
now his hair was a mess.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.170
There was something different about this time
though.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.650
Sure, he did this during all the lines for
rides he was nervous to go on, he just had

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:44.030
this look in his eye that was somehow different
when we were standing in line for Pirates.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:47.950
I told myself that he'd get over it once he'd
experienced the ride once, and tried not to

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:49.640
make a big deal out it.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.430
He kept on asking me questions.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.120
“How many drops are there?

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.500
Do you get wet?

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.230
Does it go pitch black?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.880
Will the Pirates touch you?”

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.640
I just about couldn't take anymore incessant
pestering by the time we'd reached the front

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.650
of the line.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.420
Our boat pulled into the station and we filed
in, sticking with the usual seating arrangement

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.710
of Nick, Sean, then me.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:12.530
But then, Sean had jumped out of his seat
and crossed over to the right side of the

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.530
station.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.530
“I…

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.130
I don't wanna go.”

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.130
He stuttered.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.130
“Come on…”

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.130
I told him.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.200
“This ride’s nothing.”

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.230
Then his friend Nick jumped out and offered
to skip the ride with him.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.230
Great.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:25.890
My one bargaining tool was gone.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:26.890
“You can go.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.720
We'll meet you by the exit.”

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.380
I considered this for a moment.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.190
Mom would probably kill me if she knew I'd
let them go by themselves.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:37.980
Still, we'd waited for so long, and this was
one of my favorite rides.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.680
He was 11 years old now.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.680
And they were together.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.330
What's the worst that could happen?

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.330
“Fine.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.730
But you stay together.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.530
And meet me right by the exit.”

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.000
And with that, Nick and Sean disappeared into
the dark of the synthetic bayou.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.100
My boat took off.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.650
I was in the third row.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.040
In front of me were two parents and their
young son.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:02.580
And the front row was occupied by two kids,
about Sean's age, and their Mom.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:06.010
Seeing them momentarily made me regret leaving
Sean and Nick on their own.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.940
Perhaps they weren't old enough to look after
themselves yet.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.620
I made myself wash that thought away with
the soothing sounds of the swamp.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.880
(Sounds)

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:22.920
But as those sounds faded away, I felt a chill
go up my spine.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:29.259
“Ye come seekin’ adventure and salty ol’
Pirates, eh?

00:04:29.259 --> 00:04:34.490
Sure ye come to the proper place.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:39.610
But keep a weather eye open, mates, and hold
on tight, with both hands if you please…

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:47.080
there be squalls ahead, and Davy Jones waiting
for them what don't obey..

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.080
”

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.020
The kid in front of me grabbed onto his Dad's
arm for comfort.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.020
This was it.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.870
The first and biggest drop that the ride had
to offer.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.819
I threw my hands into the air and the kids
around me screamed as we plunged down into

00:04:57.819 --> 00:05:00.759
the darkness…

00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:06.849
only… something was not right when we splashed
down at the bottom.

00:05:06.849 --> 00:05:09.590
For one, it was still pitch black.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:12.999
Usually this part of the ride was lit with
blue and green colored lights that accented

00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:14.740
the inside of the cavern.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.240
The other difference was the lack of music.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:21.210
The bottom of the drop should be accompanied
by the song, A Pirate’s Life For Me.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:25.520
But instead all I could hear was the crashing
of water around me, echoing in every which

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.110
direction off the cavernous walls.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:32.900
I could no longer see the kids and parents
in front of me, as the area was pitch black,

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.389
but I could hear one them crying, and the
parents trying to comfort him.

00:05:36.389 --> 00:05:39.450
To be fair, that kid had every right to be
scared.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.190
Because as anyone who’s ridden the ride
knows there was a second drop coming, but

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.819
with no light or sound to tip us off as to
when it would happen, it could come at any

00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:48.819
moment.

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:52.660
All we had to go on was the crashing sounds
of the waterfall getting louder and louder.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:58.080
I felt my stomach drop hard, when it happened,
and I have to say, those drops feel much faster

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.050
and scarier in the complete dark.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.292
But after that, we just floated.

00:06:04.292 --> 00:06:06.629
I honestly could barely tell if we were going
anywhere.

00:06:06.629 --> 00:06:11.069
I know we had drifted away from the drop but
even as my eyes adjusted to the dark, I still

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:13.229
could not see much of anything.

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:17.449
I began to wonder if it was just the show
that was broken, or if the entire ride system

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:18.449
was down.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:22.520
My biggest fear was getting stuck on the ride
and Sean and Nick, not knowing what to do

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.520
wandering off.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.090
There was some chatter from the other guests.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.169
The kids asking what would happen.

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:31.479
The parents and myself trying to figure out
what to do.

00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:33.310
There was no cell reception.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:37.270
At one point we decided to call out.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.520
“Hello?”

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.960
No response, though I knew it was a longshot.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:45.120
We discussed the possibility of a power outage,
and what would happen if that were the case.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.520
How long would be be trapped down here?

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.020
Was it a good idea to go out on foot?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:54.689
Before we could come to a decision, suddenly,
the power seemed to kick back on all at once,

00:06:54.689 --> 00:06:57.810
and that was when probably the most terrifying.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:58.960
Thing.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.110
Happened.

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:04.909
The voice chanting, “Dead Men Tell No Tales”
boomed over us as a strobe light viciously

00:07:04.909 --> 00:07:06.780
overloaded my retinas.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:10.379
The shock of those two events would have been
enough to give someone a heart attack, but

00:07:10.379 --> 00:07:13.930
what I saw in the light is something that
still chills me to this day.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.710
We were at the shipwreck scene.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:19.569
If you’re not familiar with the ride, there’s
a portion where a strobe light occasionally

00:07:19.569 --> 00:07:23.870
illuminates the image of a skeleton gripping
the steering wheel of a destroyed vessel during

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.530
a heavy rainstorm.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:29.199
The scene is mostly a dark silhouette in front
of the the stormy night sky.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:33.150
But when lightning struck, there was someone
standing there.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.150
Staring at us.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.930
And I can tell you right now, this was no
animatronic.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.030
I obviously didn’t get a great look at him
in that short split-second, but he had a big

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.030
bushy beard.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:45.449
It was hard to tell if he was even dressed
to fit the ride, or if he was just some guy

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:47.039
in a dark jacket.

00:07:47.039 --> 00:07:51.999
Despite only having seen him for a fraction
of a second, I couldn’t get his fiery stare

00:07:51.999 --> 00:07:53.810
out of my head.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:58.340
Almost immediately after this, the lights
shut back off and the audio slowed to a stop.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:02.150
It was pretty clear at this point that they
were having power issues.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.050
Again, if you’re not familiar with the ride’s
layout, the shipwreck scene is normally only

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:10.120
like a minute past that second drop, but we
had already been floating for at least five

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.319
minutes at this point.

00:08:11.319 --> 00:08:13.319
Here’s the other thing that bothered me.

00:08:13.319 --> 00:08:15.229
That guy I saw.

00:08:15.229 --> 00:08:18.870
If that was in fact an employee of the park…
wouldn’t he be helping us out right now

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.879
to evacuate the ride?

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:24.650
Knowing that there aren’t usually any live
actors on the ride gave me an uneasy feeling

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.319
about seeing the guy.

00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:30.129
I wasn’t sure if any of the others on my
boat have noticed, but I didn’t want to

00:08:30.129 --> 00:08:34.719
freak out those kids any more than they already
were, so I didn’t say anything.

00:08:34.719 --> 00:08:39.590
We sat in near silence for probably another
10 minutes.

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:40.640
(sounds)

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.090
I tried using my phone light to scope things
out and see where we were.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:48.870
I was almost shaking at the thought of seeing
that guy again in the dark.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.910
I surveyed around.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.030
(sound)

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.160
Great.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.290
So we had only moved backwards from where
we were before.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:01.480
After turning my phone light back off, we
sat a short while longer, and as we waited,

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:06.780
I started to notice a splashing that seemed
to be coming from behind us.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.500
Moments later, it started to become clear.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.680
Someone was trudging through the water behind
us, and coming for our boat.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:17.650
I didn’t want to alarm the other riders,
so at first I ignored it, hoping it was in

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.870
my head or something and that it would just
go away.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:25.210
But it became quite obvious to everyone involved
that there was a person walking directly towards

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.240
our boat.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.990
I looked back and my eyes were again met with
an uncomfortably bright light, this time a

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.820
flashlight that was pointed up directly in
my face.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:35.380
My heart was beating out of my chest.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:38.380
Who was this guy? Was it the guy I had seen
earlier?

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:42.160
My questions were soon answered, by a voice
that called out to us.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.990
“Hey guys, my name is Captain Carter.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:46.690
Sorry about the inconvenience.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.820
We’re actually experiencing a park-wide
power outage right now, so I’m gonna ask

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:55.690
that you and your entire crew stay seated,
while I guide your ship back to safety.”

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.640
The voice was coming from a costumed cast
member wearing thigh high rubber boots and

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.150
just walking through the middle of the ride
track.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:06.380
She actually ended up just pushing our boat
way across the ride to the market scene where

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:10.510
several other ride boats were lined up and
many other cast members with flashlights were

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:14.090
assisting them to a hidden stairway, leading
out of the ride.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:17.900
I have to admit, they had a pretty efficient
system for getting people out in the event

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.180
of an emergency.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.830
Two men in uniform were helping hoist guests
out of the boat and sending them down to the

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.250
emergency exit.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:28.410
While I waited for my turn I had one question
weighing heavy on my mind.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.750
“Uhm excuse me?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.160
Captain Carter was it?

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.160
“Yes?”

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:33.740
“I have a question.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.620
When the power came back on earlier for just
a couple seconds…”

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.620
“Uh-huh…”

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.440
“I saw a guy standing there.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.440
Just looking at us.”

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:44.590
“Oh, that must have been one of the animatronics
coming back on.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.340
Sometimes it takes a few minutes after a shutdown.”

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:50.650
“Are there any animatronics over in that
area though?

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.660
Like, by the shipwreck?”

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.660
“Uhhhhh, I’m not sure.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.100
I don’t think so, but I’d have to check
on that.”

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:02.050
I would later take to YouTube to confirm what
I saw was not an animatronic.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.190
The uniformed guys then helped me out of the
boat.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:08.050
I thought I must be one of the few Disney
guests to ever get to walk the area of the

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:09.350
ride scene on foot.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.530
I was the last guest to evacuate the ride
and I was advised to use my phone light, and

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:18.080
follow along the cobblestone until I reached
a staircase which I was to use to exit.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.800
I made it to the stairs…

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:25.240
when I felt that same chill go up my spine...
just as I had before the power had gone out.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.120
I looked all around me.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:31.330
On my left was the backside of the fake walls
that made up the ride’s backdrop.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.720
It seemed to be used as a little storage area.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:37.550
The other side was a little pathway for staff
members blocked by a ladder.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.720
So I continued ahead, up towards another staircase.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:46.610
But before I exited the ride area... before
I got back to my brother and his friend…

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:49.750
Before I walked them back to the car, not
letting them out of my sight for even the

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.800
slightest moment…

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.530
Before I left that ride area…

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:59.870
I heard the faintest sound emanating in the
distance behind me.

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:05.020
[banjo sounds]

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:15.430
Thanks for listening to Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:20.490
Your total today comes out to $117, but if
you like this video right now, I’ll waive

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:24.710
that fee and give you everything you just
listened to, absolutely free.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:29.890
I’d like to give a huge thank you to my
collaborators on this video: OST Maker for

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:35.930
composing the music; Elixir, Margbot and Don’t
